From e02ba11902c46bda790d28cd46859aec1f5fce8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:51:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Thompson: re-close graupel gains after the limiters

Rain collecting ice and cold rain collecting snow conserve water by
construction (prg_rci = pri_rci + prr_rci; prr_rcs + prs_rcs + prg_rcs = 0)
until the clips and the ice/rain/snow rate limiters rescale the losses but
not the graupel gains. Recompute prg_rci and (below 0 C) prg_rcs after the
limiters. Below 0 C the snow gain from rain-snow collection is first capped
at the rain lost to it, so that prg_rcs cannot go negative when the rain
limiter acts.

Measured (C96 control_p8_ugwpv1, on top of the mass-basis fix): removes a
source that is large during spin-up (0.76 % of grid-scale precipitation in
the first 6 h of a cold start) and about 0.03 % afterwards. Alone on
develop in the regional and convection-allowing tests: precipitation -1.0 to
-4.1 % (regional_control +0.3 %), the water these terms created.

Part of a water-conservation project for UFS physics (NOAA GML / CIRES).

AI-assisted: written with Claude Opus 5.5; reviewed by author
---
 physics/MP/Thompson/module_mp_thompson.F90 | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/physics/MP/Thompson/module_mp_thompson.F90 b/physics/MP/Thompson/module_mp_thompson.F90
index 7b7d460c..fdd5ac04 100644
--- a/physics/MP/Thompson/module_mp_thompson.F90
+++ b/physics/MP/Thompson/module_mp_thompson.F90
@@ -3161,6 +3161,8 @@ module module_mp_thompson
             prr_rcs(k) = prr_rcs(k) * ratio
             prr_rcg(k) = prr_rcg(k) * ratio
          endif
+         ! snow cannot gain more from rain-snow collection than the rain loses to it
+         if (temp(k).lt.T_0 .and. prs_rcs(k).gt.-prr_rcs(k)) prs_rcs(k) = -prr_rcs(k)
 
 !>  - Snow conservation.
          sump = prs_sde(k) - prs_ihm(k) - prr_sml(k) &
@@ -3192,6 +3194,9 @@ module module_mp_thompson
          ratio = min( ABS(prr_rcg(k)), ABS(prg_rcg(k)) )
          prr_rcg(k) = ratio * SIGN(1.0, SNGL(prr_rcg(k)))
          prg_rcg(k) = -prr_rcg(k)
+         ! graupel gains must match the (possibly limited) losses that feed them
+         prg_rci(k) = pri_rci(k) + prr_rci(k)
+         if (temp(k).lt.T_0) prg_rcs(k) = -(prr_rcs(k) + prs_rcs(k))
          if (temp(k).gt.T_0) then
             ratio = min( ABS(prr_rcs(k)), ABS(prs_rcs(k)) )
             prr_rcs(k) = ratio * SIGN(1.0, SNGL(prr_rcs(k)))
